Qwen3.8-27B on TensorFold v0.6.5: a pinned attention-cache pool for the concurrent decoder (one GPU). Ported from patch
0005-qwen27-kv-pool.patch of the Qwen3.8-27B-DGX-Spark-TensorFold recipe (against v0.6.0, Apache-2.0, a modification of
TensorFold by the TensorFold contributors); new in the port: --vision-offload no longer empties torch's cache (which
would hand the pool back) while a pool is set.
TENSORFOLD_KV_POOL_GIB=78 reserves that much cache memory once startup is done (one block, touched so its pages are
real, freed into torch's allocator and never released: the decoder's cache-trimming calls become no-ops). The streams'
caches and the kept prompt states grow inside it; the memory gate counts what torch holds beyond the weights and fixed
buffers against the pool instead of asking the host's free memory. The startup estimate counts the pool instead of
caches that grow. Unset, nothing changes. Applies after 0003.

